   "liczba": false
  },
  "You have two ways to get rid of the need to confirm the UAC dialog whenever you deploy mods, both have drawbacks!\nFirst, you can go to windows Settings -> \"Update & Security\" -> \"For developers\" and enable \"Developer Mode\". This will however also install some software and services that you don't actually need as a regular user. If you want to go this route you should cancel now, quit Vortex and restart after enabling \"Developer Mode\".\nThe other option is for Vortex to set up a global task in windows that has the increased permissions and can be triggered by your regular account. You'd only have to confirm the UAC dialog once (every time you toggle this setting). The drawback is that this might be a security risk if anyone gets control of your windows account.": {
